20	// Task execution is two similar, consecutive phases — deterministic CODE-WORK,
21	// then AGENTIC WORK — and the field names say so. Neither phase is named for
22	// the other: the code phase is not preparation for the agent, it is the first
23	// of two peers, and a task may declare only it.
24	//
25	// Two renames have reached these fields (2026-08-06 agent_preprocessing →
26	// prework, 2026-08-18 prework → code-work); both legacy spellings stay accepted
27	// here, since a consumer's own local packs rename on their own clock. Every
28	// legacy key maps straight to today's canonical name rather than to its
29	// immediate successor, so a declaration written for the oldest vocabulary
30	// normalizes in one pass. Canonical names win when both are present.
31	const LEGACY_FIELDS = {
32	  agent_preprocessing: 'code_work',
33	  agent_preprocessing_timeout: 'code_work_timeout',
34	  prework: 'code_work',
35	  prework_timeout: 'code_work_timeout',
